    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d397">

                <pb facs="0537" n="525" sameAs="frus:frus1946v08/pg525"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 PW/5–3146: Circular telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Certain Diplomatic and
                        Consular Officers</hi><anchor n="54" xml:id="d397-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-05-31T08:00:00-04:00">May 31, 1946—8 a.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Pauley reports Chistiakov has prearranged tour for mission with all movements
                    heavily guarded. Mission not allowed visit two major <pb facs="0538" n="526"
                        xml:id="pg526"/> areas north Korea, denied access certain plants other
                    areas, not permitted split into groups to accomplish mission in 5 days allowed.
                    Sovs forbidden members take any photographs on official trips.<anchor n="55"
                        xml:id="d397-f2"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Byrnes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d397-f1" n="54" type="source" xml:id="d397-f1-content">
                <p>At Berlin, London, and Paris.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d397-f2" n="55" xml:id="d397-f2-content">
                <p>Mr. Pauley left Seoul for Mukden, Manchuria, on June 14.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
